TARGET: lib/arborist/load-actual.js
REASON: Upstream 10.0.2 removed the ActualLoader constructor that initialises
the realpath and stat caches (Symbol.for("realpathCache") / ("statCache")).
In the full npm CLI these caches are likely initialised by the rebuild or
reify mixin, but cdxgen only loads loadActual and loadVirtual.  Without
initialisation, realpathCached() receives undefined for rpcache and throws
"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'has')".  The 9.1.4 vendored
tree had this constructor; restoring it is a cdxgen-specific fix for the
stripped mixin set.

---
SEARCH:
  class ActualLoader extends cls {
    #actualTree;
REPLACE:
  class ActualLoader extends cls {
    constructor(options) {
      super(options);
      const cwd = process.cwd();
      this[_rpcache] = new Map([[cwd, cwd]]);
      this[_stcache] = new Map();
    }

    #actualTree;
